  "title": "Jayavarman VII",
  "summary": "Jayavarman VII was a Khmer king whose reign is dated 1181 to 1218 by the Musée Guimet and 1181 to c. 1220 by another source. His accession followed a troubled period ending in 1177 with a Cham siege of Angkor. He made Mahāyāna Buddhism the state religion, and the Bayon was built and rebuilt under him.",
